# PUBLIC build-time configuration. Committed on purpose.
#
# Everything here is a NEXT_PUBLIC_* value, which Next inlines into the client
# bundle at build time - these strings are already visible to anyone who views
# the page source, so keeping them in git costs nothing and makes the build
# reproducible anywhere (local, CI, Cloudflare Workers Builds) without a
# dashboard form being the single source of truth.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER put a secret in this file, or in any .env file in this repo.
#
# Server-side values (DATABASE_URL, UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_*, NOTION_API_KEY) are
# Worker secrets, set with `wrangler secret put`, and they are deliberately NOT
# here: OpenNext snapshots .env FILES into .open-next/cloudflare/next-env.mjs
# and ships that inside the Worker. scripts/cf-build.mjs hides this file for the
# duration of the build so the snapshot stays empty, but that is a safety net,
# not a licence - a secret added here would still be readable to anyone with
# repo access.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_ID=G-GH95JVWL77
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=tpoy4vtmng
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDFRONT_URL=https://d3uhdrv85r0gh2.cloudfront.net
NEXT_PUBLIC_INVISIBLE_MODE=false
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_MODE=true
